 "literal": "If moving away, it burns; when approaching, it is cool; fire, where did she obtain, this woman?",
 "translation": "When I move away, it burns; when I draw near, it cools. Where did this woman get such a strange fire?",
 "modern": "நான் விலகிச் சென்றால் சுடுகிறது; நெருங்கி வந்தால் குளிர்கிறது. இத்தகைய விந்தையான நெருப்பை இவள் எங்கே பெற்றாள்?",
 "explanation": "The lover marvels at the unique nature of his beloved's embrace. Ordinary fire burns when one gets close and loses its heat when one moves away. However, the fire of love he feels from her does the exact opposite: it scorches him with longing when they are apart, but cools and comforts him when they are together. He playfully wonders where she found such a paradoxical fire.",
